  "dry_snp_activity": "Large sizes remain popular among Greek shipowners. On the Newcastlemax sector the “Mineral Charlie” - 205K/2012 HHIC and “Mineral Maureen” - 205K/2012 HHIC were sold for USD 81.6 mills enbloc to Greek buyers. Greek buyers acquired also the Capesize “Courageous”- 181K/2016 SWS for USD 50.5 mills, while also seem to be behind from the sale of “Stella Hope” - 180K/2016 Dalian which was sold for USD 49.5 mills. Moving down the sizes the Kamsarmax “Livia Rose” - 82K/2018 Tsuneishi Zhoushan was sold for USD 35.6 mills to clients of HMM. On the Supramax sector, the “Maine Dream” - 58K/2012 Tsuneishi Cebu found new owners for USD 19.3 mills. Last but not least, the Handysize “Gold Dust” - 28K/2012 Imabari was sold for USD12 mills to Vietnamese buyers.",
  "wet_snp_activity": "The tanker S&P activity was low this week, with only 4 sales to report. On the VLCC sector, Greek buyers acquired the Scrubber fitted “C. Prosperity” - 314K/2009 HHI for USD 53.5 mills. The Scrubber fitted Suezmax “Front Thor” - 157K/2010 Jiangsu Rongsheng changed hands for excess USD 48 mills. Finally, on the MR2 sector, the “Avon” - 50K/2019 HMD found new owners for USD 45.5 mills basis TC attached at USD 23.5k/day for 5 years.\n\nNAME DWT YEAR COUNTRY YARD BUYERS PRICE ($ mills) COMMENTS",
